ch('HSD_ByteCodeEval','game_mapping','RObj expEvaluate dispatches to HSD_ByteCodeEval when exp->is_bytecode is set and otherwise calls the native expression function. It passes arg_buf and exp->nb_args, converts selected output types to radians, then calls update_func. This canonical caller supports the RObj-expression relationship; actual in-game reachability is not established by this review.')
ch('FILE','game_mapping','Provides the bytecode branch of RObj expEvaluate. The caller selects bytecode or native function via exp->is_bytecode and forwards the evaluated value through update_func after optional angular conversion. Runtime reachability and absence of other gameplay uses are not proved by this bounded source review.')
ch('HSD_ByteCodeEval','inferred_type','Signature float HSD_ByteCodeEval(u8* bytecode, const f32* args, s32 nb_args). Instructions use one-, two- or four-byte big-endian immediates; stack nodes carry untagged 32-bit words reinterpreted as int, float or pointer in the target ABI. Argument loads assert operand < nb_args, but operand is u32 so negative nb_args converts to unsigned. There is no stream length parameter or general pointer/operand validation.')
ch('HSD_ByteCodeEval','state_behavior','Alternates opcode fetch and immediate collection. Opcode 3 consumes a raw nonzero word as a condition and pops it after an optional unsigned forward skip; opcode 4 always skips; opcode 1 reads top bits as f32 and frees all nodes. Most operand accesses assert stack depth, but opcode 5 repeatedly removes nodes and HSD_SListRemove(NULL) returns NULL, so over-discard does not assert. Missing duplicate depth, opcode 0xFF after one immediate byte, and unknown opcodes panic. Argument comparison is unsigned; byte-stream bounds, integer arithmetic and math-domain errors are not generally validated. Random opcodes advance the shared RNG.')
ch('FILE','state_behavior','The local stack starts empty and decoding alternates between opcode fetch and one-, two- or four-byte immediate collection. Normal return frees the entire stack. Many invalid accesses assert or panic, but discard past an empty stack is tolerated by HSD_SListRemove. There is no input-length bound, opcode budget, signed argument-count validation, arithmetic overflow/divisor validation or recovery cleanup path for panics. Random operations mutate the shared generator.')
